---
title: "Krewire — One Go Framework for Every Workload"
description: "Unified Go Framework for every workload — app, cli, site, book, worker, service, infra, runtime. One CLI kiw, one config krewire.yaml."
layout: Landing
---

<!-- HERO SECTION -->
<section class="hero">
  <div class="hero-inner">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <div class="eyebrow">
        <span>◈</span>
        <span>Unified Go Framework · v0.1.0 · Open Source</span>
      </div>
      <h1>One Go Framework.<br>Every Workload.</h1>
      <p class="lead">From single-binary web monoliths to interactive TUIs, high-speed static sites, book pipelines, background workers, microservices, cloud infra, and Go WebAssembly runtimes — build everything in Go with one CLI <code>kiw</code> and zero JS fatigue.</p>
      
      <!-- QUICK START COMMAND BOX -->
      <div class="quick-terminal">
        <div class="terminal-bar">
          <span class="term-prompt">$</span>
          <code>kiw new my-app --site && cd my-app && kiw serve</code>
          <button class="btn-copy" onclick="copyCmd(this, 'kiw new my-app --site && cd my-app && kiw serve')">Copy</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="ctas">
        <a class="btn primary large" href="/docs/getting-started">Get Started — 5 Min →</a>
        <a class="btn large" href="#workloads">Explore 8 Workloads ↓</a>
        <a class="btn large" href="https://github.com/krewire/krewire" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span>★</span> GitHub</a>
      </div>
      <div class="meta">Go 1.22+ · File-based routing · Scoped CSS · 100% Zero JS by default</div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-art">
      {{component "CodeWindow" .}}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- TRUST & VALUE METRICS STRIP -->
<section class="trust">
  <div class="trust-inner">
    <span class="trust-label">Unified Go Toolchain</span>
    <div class="trust-items">
      <span><b>100%</b> Go Standard Library</span>
      <span class="dot">·</span>
      <span><b>0</b> npm / 0 Bundlers</span>
      <span class="dot">·</span>
      <span><b>8</b> Workloads in 1 Binary</span>
      <span class="dot">·</span>
      <span><b>&lt; 1ms</b> Cold Starts</span>
      <span class="dot">·</span>
      <span>Single Config <code>krewire.yaml</code></span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 8 WORKLOADS SHOWCASE -->
<section class="workloads" id="workloads">
  <div class="section-inner">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="sub-badge">Unified Workload Engine</span>
      <h2>One Framework. Eight Workloads.</h2>
      <p>Stop assembling disparate frameworks for web, CLI, background queues, and infra. Krewire provides unified ergonomics, shared configuration, and zero context switching.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="workloads-grid">
      <!-- 1. APP -->
      <div class="workload-card highlight">
        <div class="card-header">
          <div class="workload-icon">▲</div>
          <span class="workload-tag primary-tag">Fullstack</span>
        </div>
        <h3>app</h3>
        <p>Fullstack web monolith — compile your web interface, HTTP routing, and API handlers into a single static Go binary.</p>
        <div class="workload-cmd"><code>kiw run</code></div>
      </div>

      <!-- 2. CLI -->
      <div class="workload-card">
        <div class="card-header">
          <div class="workload-icon">›_</div>
          <span class="workload-tag">Terminal</span>
        </div>
        <h3>cli</h3>
        <p>Command-line utilities and interactive TUIs powered by a Bubble Tea-inspired reactive terminal interface engine.</p>
        <div class="workload-cmd"><code>kiw build --cli</code></div>
      </div>

      <!-- 3. SITE -->
      <div class="workload-card">
        <div class="card-header">
          <div class="workload-icon">◧</div>
          <span class="workload-tag">SSG</span>
        </div>
        <h3>site</h3>
        <p>High-performance static site generator with file-based routing, scoped <code>.kiw</code> components, and zero client-side JS.</p>
        <div class="workload-cmd"><code>kiw build --site</code></div>
      </div>

      <!-- 4. BOOK -->
      <div class="workload-card">
        <div class="card-header">
          <div class="workload-icon">≡</div>
          <span class="workload-tag">Publishing</span>
        </div>
        <h3>book</h3>
        <p>Turn markdown manuscripts and technical manuals into structured documentation books with automatic indexing via <code>mdbind</code>.</p>
        <div class="workload-cmd"><code>kiw build --book</code></div>
      </div>

      <!-- 5. WORKER -->
      <div class="workload-card">
        <div class="card-header">
          <div class="workload-icon">⚙</div>
          <span class="workload-tag">Async</span>
        </div>
        <h3>worker</h3>
        <p>Asynchronous job queues, scheduled cron tasks, retry policies, backoff timers, and dead-letter queues via <code>framework/worker</code>.</p>
        <div class="workload-cmd"><code>kiw run --worker</code></div>
      </div>

      <!-- 6. SERVICE -->
      <div class="workload-card">
        <div class="card-header">
          <div class="workload-icon">⬢</div>
          <span class="workload-tag">Microservice</span>
        </div>
        <h3>service</h3>
        <p>Distributed microservice architecture with service discovery, API gateway routing, rate limiting, and OpenTelemetry tracing.</p>
        <div class="workload-cmd"><code>kiw run --service</code></div>
      </div>

      <!-- 7. INFRA -->
      <div class="workload-card">
        <div class="card-header">
          <div class="workload-icon">☁</div>
          <span class="workload-tag">Cloud IaC</span>
        </div>
        <h3>infra</h3>
        <p>Provider-agnostic infrastructure-as-code compiling directly to AWS, GCP, or Kubernetes specifications from Go declarations.</p>
        <div class="workload-cmd"><code>kiw infra apply</code></div>
      </div>

      <!-- 8. RUNTIME -->
      <div class="workload-card">
        <div class="card-header">
          <div class="workload-icon">◈</div>
          <span class="workload-tag">WASM</span>
        </div>
        <h3>runtime</h3>
        <p>Compile Go into WebAssembly with virtual DOM diffing, reactive interactive islands, and partial client hydration.</p>
        <div class="workload-cmd"><code>kiw build --wasm</code></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- THREE STEPS TO PRODUCTION -->
<section class="how">
  <div class="section-inner">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="sub-badge">Developer Workflow</span>
      <h2>From Zero to Production in 3 Commands</h2>
      <p>No toolchain fatigue, no breaking npm dependency trees, and zero build configuration hurdles.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="steps-grid">
      <div class="step-card">
        <div class="step-top">
          <div class="step-number">1</div>
          <span class="step-tag">Scaffold</span>
        </div>
        <h3>kiw new</h3>
        <p>Generate a production-ready project template for any workload in under one second.</p>
        <pre class="term-pre"><code>kiw new my-site --site
cd my-site</code></pre>
      </div>

      <div class="step-card">
        <div class="step-top">
          <div class="step-number">2</div>
          <span class="step-tag">Develop</span>
        </div>
        <h3>kiw dev</h3>
        <p>Instant hot-reload local development server with file-based routing and scoped CSS updates.</p>
        <pre class="term-pre"><code>kiw dev
# ⚡ Ready at http://localhost:3000</code></pre>
      </div>

      <div class="step-card">
        <div class="step-top">
          <div class="step-number">3</div>
          <span class="step-tag">Deploy</span>
        </div>
        <h3>kiw deploy</h3>
        <p>Compile into a single static binary or static asset bundle and ship to GitHub Pages or Docker.</p>
        <pre class="term-pre"><code>kiw deploy --target gh-pages
# ✓ Deployed successfully!</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ARCHITECTURAL PILLARS / WHY KREWIRE -->
<section class="why">
  <div class="section-inner">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="sub-badge">Architecture & Philosophy</span>
      <h2>Go-First. Progressive. Zero Bloat.</h2>
      <p>Built for engineers who value compilation speed, predictable deployments, and maintainable software architecture.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="why-grid">
      <div class="why-card">
        <div class="why-icon-box">◈</div>
        <h3>Pure Go Toolchain</h3>
        <p>No Node.js, no npm dependencies, and no bundler configuration. Your entire application compiles with standard Go tooling into clean, self-contained binaries.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="why-card">
        <div class="why-icon-box">◧</div>
        <h3>Scoped .kiw Components</h3>
        <p>Combines YAML frontmatter, standard Go HTML templates, and scoped <code>&lt;style&gt;</code> blocks. CSS classes never leak outside their component boundary.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="why-card">
        <div class="why-icon-box">⚡</div>
        <h3>Progressive Scaling</h3>
        <p>Start as a lightweight static site, grow into a fullstack web monolith, then seamlessly extract background workers and microservices — all within the same ecosystem.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="why-card">
        <div class="why-icon-box">🛡</div>
        <h3>Enterprise Resilience</h3>
        <p>Engineered with production defaults: structured JSON logging, distributed tracing, health checks, circuit breakers, and graceful shutdown out of the box.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- COMPONENT DSL SHOWCASE -->
<section class="showcase">
  <div class="section-inner">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="sub-badge">Component DSL</span>
      <h2>Write Pages as Clean .kiw Components</h2>
      <p>The elegance of Svelte and Astro brought to Go. Frontmatter + HTML + scoped CSS in one intuitive file.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="showcase-grid">
      <div class="showcase-code-panel">
