          <div class="panel-dots">
            <span class="p-dot r"></span>
            <span class="p-dot y"></span>
            <span class="p-dot g"></span>
          </div>
          <span class="panel-file">pages/index.kiw</span>
        </div>
        <pre class="panel-pre"><code><span class="c">---</span>
<span class="k">title:</span> "Welcome to Krewire"
<span class="k">layout:</span> Landing
<span class="k">workload:</span> site
<span class="c">---</span>

<span class="t">&lt;section class="welcome"&gt;</span>
  <span class="t">&lt;h1&gt;</span>{{"{{"}}.Title{{"}}"}}<span class="t">&lt;/h1&gt;</span>
  <span class="t">&lt;p&gt;</span>Compiled Go speed with zero runtime bloat.<span class="t">&lt;/p&gt;</span>
<span class="t">&lt;/section&gt;</span>

<span class="t">&lt;style&gt;</span>
.welcome { padding: 40px 0; text-align: center; }
h1 { color: var(--primary); font-weight: 900; }
p  { font-size: 15px; color: var(--muted); }
<span class="t">&lt;/style&gt;</span></code></pre>
        <div class="panel-footer">
          <a class="btn primary" href="/docs/dsl">Explore DSL Syntax →</a>
          <a class="btn" href="/docs/getting-started">Read the Docs</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="showcase-feature-panel">
        <div class="feature-panel-card">
          <div class="fpc-head">
            <span class="fpc-badge">Scoping</span>
            <h3>Why Scoped CSS in Go?</h3>
          </div>
          <p>Every <code>.kiw</code> component receives automatic <code>data-kiw-component</code> scope hashing at build time. No CSS collisions, no naming gymnastics, zero runtime cost.</p>
          <ul class="fpc-list">
            <li><span>✓</span> <b>Scoped by Default:</b> Styles remain strictly isolated to the component.</li>
            <li><span>✓</span> <b>Global CSS via <code>:root</code>:</b> Theme tokens cascade cleanly across layouts.</li>
            <li><span>✓</span> <b>No Bundler Required:</b> Built directly by the Go compiler without npm.</li>
            <li><span>✓</span> <b>Light & Dark Mode:</b> Native token switching via <code>data-theme</code>.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

